# Git Workflow

## Branch Naming

```
feature/{short-description}
fix/{short-description}
refactor/{short-description}
```

Examples: `feature/message-search`, `fix/invite-validation`

## Commit Messages

Format: `type(scope): description`

```
feat(auth): add JWT access and refresh token flow
fix(gateway): handle reconnection race condition
refactor(guild): extract permission checks to middleware
test(message): add pagination edge case tests
chore(infra): update docker-compose postgres version
docs: update CLAUDE.md with voice architecture
```

Types: `feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `test`, `chore`, `docs`
Scopes: `auth`, `guild`, `channel`, `message`, `gateway`, `presence`, `voice`, `friend`, `storage`, `infra`, `frontend`

## PR Convention

One PR per task. Title matches the commit convention. PR body should have:

```
## Summary
- What was added/changed and why

## Test plan
- How it was tested (commands, manual steps)
```

## Rules

- Never commit `.env` files, secrets, or credentials
- Always run `go test ./...` before committing backend changes
- Always run `npm run lint` before committing frontend changes
- Keep PRs small and focused — one logical change per PR
